      <sectiondef kind="define">
      <memberdef kind="define" id="wsh__shell__promptwait_8h_1acdd6e940885e4e5d9a59450574806c59" prot="public" static="no">
        <name>WSH_SHELL_PROMPT_WAIT_HINT_RETRIES</name>
        <initializer>3</initializer>
        <briefdescription>
<para>How many rejected keystrokes still reprint the prompt hint. </para>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para>A prompt-wait is modal: nothing the user types reaches the command line, so the hint is the only explanation. Repeating it on every keystroke floods whatever else is streaming, so it is repeated a few times and then the wait goes quiet. The bell keeps sounding on every rejection regardless. </para>
        </detaileddescription>
        <inbodydescription>
        </inbodydescription>
